    "details": "<p><strong>Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 23 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> 11:00 AM &ndash; 1:30 PM</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> Registrar Office, I.T.S Engineering College, Greater Noida</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee:</strong> ₹200/team</li>\n<li><strong>Prize Pool:</strong> ₹10,000</li>\n<li><strong>Coordinator:</strong> Miss Riddhi Chahar</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Description</strong></p>\n<p>Poster Exhibition at TechTrix'26 provides a platform for grassroots innovators to present innovative posters and paintings addressing real-world problems across software and hardware domains. Participants explain their ideas and technical concepts to a jury, demonstrating the relevance and practical application of their work.</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Team Size &amp; Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>2 participants per team</li>\n<li>Open to undergraduate/postgraduate students and eligible participants from colleges/institutions</li>\n<li>Valid college/institutional ID is mandatory</li>\n<li>Only registered participants may compete; one participant cannot be registered in two teams for the same event</li>\n<li>Team composition cannot be changed after the registration deadline without written approval from the Event Coordinator</li>\n<li>The registered team captain is the official point of contact</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Poster Format</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Recommended Size: A1, portrait orientation</li>\n<li>Must clearly include: Title, Problem Statement, Methodology, Results, Applications, References</li>\n<li>Figures, diagrams, and photographs may be used where they support the technical explanation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Presentation Format</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Each participant/team must explain their poster to the jury</li>\n<li>The jury may ask technical, application-based, and problem/solution-related questions &mdash; participants should be prepared to explain both the technical content and practical relevance of their work</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Criteria</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Weightage</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Technical Content</td>\n<td>25%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Innovation</td>\n<td>20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Depth of Work / Research</td>\n<td>20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Visual Communication</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Practical Application</td>\n<td>10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Presentation &amp; Q&amp;A</td>\n<td>10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>100%</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> A visually attractive poster without meaningful technical content will not receive a high technical score. All copied material must be properly referenced.</p>\n<p><strong>Disqualification</strong></p>\n<p><strong>A team may be disqualified for:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Receiving external assistance during the competition</li>\n<li>Plagiarism or cheating (including uncredited copied material)</li>\n<li>Misconduct with judges, volunteers, or organisers</li>\n<li>Misrepresentation of participant identity</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Event Jury/Organizing Committee holds final authority on judging, penalties, disqualification, and interpretation of rules.</p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"6347\" data-end=\"6410\">NOTE-: Registration Fees are not refundable.</strong></p>",
